==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|totheles}}, {{m|enm|toþeles}}, from {{inh|en|ang|tōþlēas}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*tanþlausaz|t=toothless}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|tooth|less}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|tandeloos|t=toothless}}, {{cog|nds-de|tannlos|t=toothless}}, {{cog|de|zahnlos|t=toothless}}, {{cog|da|tandløs|t=toothless}}, {{cog|sv|tandlös|t=toothless}}, {{cog|is|tannlaus|t=toothless}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtuθləs/|/ˈtuθlɪs/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-toothless.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having no [[tooth|teeth]].
#: {{syn|en|edentate|edentulous|teethless}}
#: {{ant|en|dentate|dentiferous|dentigerous|dentulous|toothed|toothy}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''toothless''' old man}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=24 Dec 83|volume=11|number=23|journal=Gay Community News|page=8|author=Andrea Loewenstein|title="What's Freedom Without Food In Your Stomach?" -- A Trip to Haiti|text=She goes on to explain the difficulty she's having getting visas for Lawrence and for Robert, the 14-year-old who is her older brother and is, amazingly, the last child of the '''toothless''' tiny woman who buzzes around us. (I find out later that she is only in her mid-fifties.)}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[weak|Weak]]; having no ability to enforce something.
#: {{syn|en|tame|Thesaurus:weak}}
#: {{ux|en|The treaty was '''toothless''' because of the lack of participation from the undersigned.}}
#* {{RQ:Jonson Entertainment Althorp|passage=Not tell? ha! ha! I could smile / At this old and '''toothless''' wile.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021-10-10|author=Caroline Anders|title=A TikTok bone salesman’s wall of spines reignites ethical debate over selling human remains|journal=w:The Washington Post|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/science/2021/10/09/tiktok-jonsbones-human-remains-wall-spines/|passage=Bans of the sale of human remains across platforms like Facebook, Etsy, Instagram and eBay are '''toothless''' and poorly enforced, Huffer said. And when a page does get shut down, he said, it just pops up on a different website.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Zach Vasquez|title=Saturday Night Live: Charli xcx has fun in otherwise middle of the road episode|work=w:The Guardian|date=2024-11-17|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2024/nov/17/saturday-night-live-charli-xcx|issn=0261-3077|passage=The glut of moronic, Roganesque dude-bro podcasts are long overdue for mocking, but this one is '''toothless'''.}}

